    "narrative": "The LawDog offense enters today\u2019s slate with **Geraldo Perdomo** (67.71) and **Lawrence Butler** (65.73) leading the charge as our strongest plays. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a high-floor matchup against Ure\u00f1a, where his favorable position at #2 in the order and a +16% boost from the pitcher\u2019s skill profile make him a must-start. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** is poised for a breakout performance; his score is significantly elevated by a +10% park factor and a +13% dynamic platoon advantage against Jones. **Bryson Stott** (62.69) also demands attention, as his matchup against Gusto features a slow delivery window, providing a rare opportunity for **Bryson Stott** to exploit the basepaths, a critical strategic edge in our pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on **Gavin Sheets** (53.09) versus the bench depth. **Gavin Sheets** narrowly secured a spot over our remaining utility options because of his power potential batting clean-up against May, though his limited ceiling keeps him in the marginal tier. We continue to monitor the status of **Jonathan Aranda** (55.90), whose status is currently labeled as \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have projected him at #2, any movement down the order will deflate his efficiency score. We are also closely tracking **Tyler Freeman** (61.33); his score is bolstered by a +5% wind-out factor at the stadium, though facing Imanaga\u2014an elite hold pitcher\u2014creates a slight risk to our SB targets. Our primary concern remains the health of our core, as we are severely hampered by the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Will Smith** on the IL. Until those anchors return, we must rely on secondary contributors like **Masyn Winn** (53.71) to provide steady production while maintaining strict adherence to our game cap management.",
